  "text": "I'll start by reading the spec and the already-built modules so `progress.js` and `shell.js` match the existing APIs and coding style.Next I’ll read the existing modules and markup so storage keys, version checks, and CSS class names stay consistent.I’ll scan the design-system classes and sibling-app patterns next so the new files reuse what’s already there.I have the APIs and class names; next I’ll write `progress.js` and `shell.js` as ES5 IIFEs that match the brief and the modules already on disk.Writing `progress.js` first, then the shell that sits on top of it.I’ll clean a few progress.js issues (unused names, no curriculum mutation), then write `shell.js`.Chunk 3 is on disk: `progress.js` (`HRL_PROGRESS`) and `shell.js` (`HRL_SHELL`). Both are ES5-safe single IIFEs. No shell commands were run.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Exported APIs\n\n**`HRL_PROGRESS`**\n\n| Name | Parameters | Returns |\n|---|---|---|\n| `load()` | — | state object |\n| `get()` | — | current in-memory state |\n| `save()` | — | `true` if `localStorage` write succeeded, else `false` (memory fallback still holds the state) |\n| `reset()` | — | fresh default state (also saved) |\n| `storageAvailable()` | — | `boolean` |\n| `isFirstRun()` | — | `true` when `placement.done` is false and no chapter has `visited` |\n| `setPlacement(obj)` | `{ recommendedTier, role, goal, experience, theta }` | the placement object (`done: true`, `takenAt` set) |\n| `getPlacement()` | — | placement object |\n| `markVisited(chapterId)` | string | chapter record |\n| `recordQuiz(chapterId, scorePct, passed)` | string, number, boolean | `{ bestScore, completed, newlyCompleted, badgesAwarded }` |\n| `getChapter(chapterId)` | string | default-filled record (never `undefined`) |\n| `isComplete(chapterId)` | string | `boolean` |\n| `tierProgress(tierKey)` | string | `{ total, complete, pct }` (pct 0–100 integer; zeros if no curriculum) |\n| `overallProgress()` | — | `{ total, complete, pct }` |\n| `nextChapter()` | — | chapter id or `null` |\n| `BOX_INTERVALS` | — | `[1, 3, 7, 16, 35]` |\n| `addMiss(qid, nowMs)` | string, number | review entry |\n| `recordReview(qid, correct, nowMs)` | string, boolean, number | updated entry, or `null` if retired at box 5 |\n| `dueReviews(nowMs)` | number | qid array, oldest due first |\n| `reviewCounts(nowMs)` | number | `{ due, total }` |\n| `recordIq(attempt)` | `{ takenAt, bbiq, band, byTopic, answers }` | stored attempt |\n| `iqHistory()` | — | attempts, newest first |\n| `bestIq()` | — | best attempt or `null` |\n| `awardBadge(id)` | string | `true` if newly awarded |\n| `hasBadge(id)` | string | `boolean` |\n| `badges()` | — | copy of badge id array |\n| `checkTierBadges()` | — | array of newly awarded `tier-*` ids |\n| `touchStreak(nowMs)` | number | `{ current, longest, changed, badgesAwarded }` |\n| `getSetting(key)` | string | value |\n| `setSetting(key, value)` | string, any | the value |\n| `exportPayload()` | — | envelope object |\n| `exportFilename(date)` | `Date` or `'YYYY-MM-DD'` | `'homerun-learn-progress-YYYY-MM-DD.json'` |\n| `mergeState(current, incoming)` | two state objects | new merged state; neither input mutated |\n| `importPayload(obj)` | parsed envelope | `{ ok, message }` — never throws |\n| `importText(jsonString)` | string | `{ ok, message }` |\n\n**`HRL_SHELL`**\n\n| Name | Parameters | Returns |\n|---|---|---|\n| `init()` | — | — (also runs on `DOMContentLoaded`) |\n| `showView(name, opts)` | view name, optional `{ scrollToTier, chapterId, ... }` | — |\n| `openChapter(chapterId)` | string | — |\n| `openQuiz(chapterId)` | string | — |\n| `current()` | — | active view name (`'home'\\|'path'\\|'chapter'\\|'quiz'\\|'iq'\\|'review'\\|'glossary'\\|'help'`) |\n| `toast(message, kind, opts?)` | string, `'info'\\|'success'\\|'warn'\\|'error'`, optional `{ dismissible, sticky, ms }` | — |\n| `on(eventName, fn)` | string, function | — |\n| `off(eventName, fn)` | string, function | — |\n| `renderHome()` | — | — |\n| `renderSettings()` | — | — |\n\n---\n\n### 2. Default state\n\n```js\n{\n  version: HRL_VERSION.DATA_VERSION,   // '1.0' if HRL_VERSION is missing\n  placement: {\n    done: false,\n    recommendedTier: 1,\n    role: null,\n    goal: null,\n    experience: null,\n    theta: 0,\n    takenAt: null\n  },\n  chapters: {},\n  badges: [],\n  review: [],\n  iq: { attempts: [], best: null },\n  streak: { current: 0, longest: 0, lastActiveDay: null },\n  settings: { timerEnabled: true, reducedMotion: false, textSize: 'normal' }\n}\n```\n\nChapter records, when created:\n\n```js\n{ visited: false, completed: false, bestScore: 0, attempts: 0, completedAt: null, lastSeenAt: null }\n```\n\nStorage key: `'homerun-learn/progress/v1'`.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Badge id strings\n\n- `chapter-<chapterId>` — e.g. `chapter-ch01`\n- `tier-<tierKey>` — `tier-rookie`, `tier-sandlot`, `tier-diamond`, `tier-select`, `tier-elite`, `tier-promind`\n- `iq-first`\n- `iq-elite` (BBIQ ≥ 125)\n- `perfect-quiz` (chapter quiz score ≥ 100)\n- `streak-3`, `streak-7`, `streak-30`\n\n---\n\n### 4. `viewchange` payload and subscribe\n\nPayload:\n\n```js\n{ view: 'path', previous: 'home', opts: { scrollToTier: 'diamond' } }\n```\n\nSubscribe:\n\n```js\nHRL_SHELL.on('viewchange', function (e) {\n  if (e.view === 'path') { /* re-render */ }\n});\nHRL_SHELL.off('viewchange', handler);\n```\n\n`chapter` and `quiz` have no nav button; `path` stays highlighted. Focus moves to the view’s `h1`/`h2` (`tabindex=\"-1\"` set in code), then the window scrolls to top.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Calls into other `HRL_*` modules (signatures assumed)\n\n**Already present**\n\n- `HRL_VERSION.APP_VERSION` / `.DATA_VERSION` / `.MIN_COMPATIBLE_DATA_VERSION`\n- `HRL_VERSION_COMPAT.isImportCompatible(importedDataVersion)` → `{ status: 'compatible'|'migratable'|'incompatible', message, migrationPath? }`\n- `HRL_VERSION_COMPAT.applyMigrations(data, migrationPath)` → upgraded data\n- `HRL_VERSION_COMPAT.compareVersions(a, b)` → `-1|0|1`\n- `HRL_MODAL.open({ title, titleId, build: function (box, api) { ... } })` — `api.close()`, `api.el(tag, attrs, children)`\n- `HRL_MODAL.close()`\n\n**Curriculum (not loaded yet — all lookups guarded)**\n\n- `HRL_CURRICULUM.tiers` — `{ key, name, order }[]`\n- `HRL_CURRICULUM.chapters` — `{ id, tier, order, title }[]`\n\n**Later chunks**\n\n- `HRL_LEARN.renderChapter(chapterId)`\n- `HRL_LEARN.renderPath()`\n- `HRL_LEARN.renderGlossary()`\n- `HRL_QUIZ.start(chapterId)`\n- `HRL_QUIZ.renderReviewDeck()`\n- `HRL_IQ.renderIntro()`\n- `HRL_PLACEMENT.start({ skippable: true, onSkip: fn, onComplete: fn })`\n\nIf a later module is missing, the matching root (`#path-root`, `#iq-root`, etc.) gets a `.empty-state` instead of a throw.\n\n**Path scroll target:** `showView('path', { scrollToTier: 'rookie' })` looks for `[data-tier=\"rookie\"]` inside `#view-path`. `renderPath()` should put `data-tier` on each tier block.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Deviations\n\n- **`prepareImport` does not exist.** `versionCompat.js` exposes `isImportCompatible` + `applyMigrations`. Import uses those. There is also a fallback version check if `HRL_VERSION_COMPAT` is absent under Node.\n- **`toast` takes an optional third `opts`.** Used so the storage-unavailable notice can be dismissible and sticky. Kind still goes on the class as `toast toast-warn` (no new CSS file).\n- **`HRL_PLACEMENT.start` is called with `{ skippable: true, onSkip, onComplete }`.** Extra properties are ignored if chunk 7 takes no args. A visible “Start from the very beginning” skip is also on the first-run continue card.\n- **`mergeState` does not read `HRL_VERSION` or storage** (pure). Missing `version` becomes `'1.0'` from the inputs, not from the global.\n- **`progress.js` IIFE is invoked with `.call(...)`**, same pattern as `svg.js`, so `this` is bound under Node.\n- **`save()` returns `false` when only the in-memory store wrote.** State is still kept for the session; `shell.js` shows the one-time warn toast when `storageAvailable()` is false.\n- **No CSS added.** Home, settings, toasts, and the progress panel reuse existing classes (`.continue-card`, `.tier-rail-item`, `.tier-ring`, `.progress-bar`, `.toast`, `.readme-section`, `.btn`, `.empty-state`, `.visually-hidden`).",
